{
  "info": {
    "name": "Marketing Backend — Web Portal (Admin)",
    "description": "Endpoints used by the admin web portal.\n\n**Getting started**\n1. Check `baseUrl` (default http://localhost:4000/api/v1).\n2. Run **1. Auth → Login (admin)**. The token is saved automatically.\n3. Call anything else. Auth is inherited from the collection (Bearer {{accessToken}}).\n\n**Ids:** create requests save the new id (campaignId, missionId, rewardId, tierId, userId, roleId) to collection variables, so get/update/delete run against what you just created.\n\n**Permissions:** each request notes the permission it needs. The seeded super admin has all of them; admins with a staff role only have what the role grants (403 otherwise).\n\n**Responses:** success `{ status: 'success', data }`, error `{ status: 'error', error: 'message' }`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4000/api/v1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "adminmkt@dlt.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "Admin1234!",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "campaignId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "missionId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "rewardId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "redemptionId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "tierId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "roleId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "uploadedUrl",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Auth",
      "description": "Run **Login (admin)** first. Every other request uses the saved {{accessToken}} via collection-level Bearer auth.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sign in to the web portal. Saves accessToken and refreshToken to collection variables automatically.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status is 2xx', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.within(200, 299));",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.accessToken !== undefined) pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.data.accessToken);",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.refreshToken !== undefined) pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.data.refreshToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exchange the refresh token for a new token pair. Saves both automatically.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status is 2xx', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.within(200, 299));",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.accessToken !== undefined) pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.data.accessToken);",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.refreshToken !== undefined) pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.data.refreshToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
